en seat: Nancy Mace (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "South Carolina's open First District seat sits in Republican-leaning territory, and Nancy Mace's departure to run for governor leaves the GOP defending it with a first-time nominee. Most race raters call it Lean Republican, two rate it Likely Republican, and one calls it a Tossup. The district's Republican lean anchors the GOP; the midterm environment favors Democrats and partially offsets it.\n\nDemocrat Nancy Lacore, a Navy veteran, has raised roughly $4.4 million to about $560,000 for Republican Jenny Costa Honeycutt, giving her the resources to compete in this Charleston-area seat. Public polling is limited and split by sponsor: a Democratic pollster showed Lacore up three, a Republican pollster showed Honeycutt up six, and an older survey had it roughly even. Prediction markets give Democrats about a three-in-ten chance. The race is competitive, with Honeycutt holding a modest edge in the final stretch.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2812, "margin": -3.39}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2869, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2863, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3426, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2352, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2308, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2761, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3368, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2774, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2992, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2787, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.3431, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.3379, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2427, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2624, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2319, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.2563, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem":